 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "서비스 이용 (I'd like to ...)",
   "en": "Using services (I'd like to ...)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "서비스를 이용할 때는 I'd like to + 동사로 하고 싶은 일을 말합니다. 물건을 달라고 할 때는 A stamp, please.처럼 말합니다. 약국에서는 증상을 I have a + 증상으로 말하고, 복용법은 Take it twice a day처럼 명령문을 써요.",
   "en": "To use a service say I'd like to + verb. To ask for something say A stamp, please. At a pharmacy say your problem with I have a + problem, and instructions are imperatives like Take it twice a day."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "I'd like to + 동사",
     "I'd like to send a letter."
    ],
    [
     "A ~, please",
     "Two stamps, please."
    ],
    [
     "I have a ~",
     "I have a headache."
    ],
    [
     "Take ~ twice a day",
     "Take it twice a day."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "I'd like to는 I want to보다 공손합니다.",
    "en": "I'd like to is more polite than I want to."
   },
   {
    "ko": "headache처럼 증상에는 a를 씁니다.",
    "en": "Use a with symptoms: a headache."
   },
   {
    "ko": "횟수는 once, twice 다음에는 three times로 말합니다.",
    "en": "Count with once, twice, then three times."
   }
  ],
